he left out?

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.190
You know, you'd have to ask them.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:55.059
I've only looked at a bulleted summary so
far.

00:00:55.059 --> 00:00:56.820
I've not read through all of it.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.920
But certainly the Biden plan is not the green
New Deal.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:06.359
The Biden plan is, you know, what I found
good about the Biden plan in terms of the

00:01:06.359 --> 00:01:11.590
summaries that I've read, is that he's doing
what he promised to do.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:16.439
In other words, months ago, Joe Biden said,
I support the Green New Deal as a framework

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:21.029
with which I will build a plan and we'll listen
to what the Green New Deal says and consider

00:01:21.029 --> 00:01:23.609
other voices and a lot of people that I don't
believe it.

00:01:23.609 --> 00:01:24.609
I don't believe it.

00:01:24.609 --> 00:01:25.609
I don't believe it.

00:01:25.609 --> 00:01:30.340
And the Biden plan integrates some of the
milestones and guidelines of the Green New

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:35.069
Deal into a plan that, to be clear, is not
the green New Deal.

00:01:35.069 --> 00:01:40.139
But what I'm pleased by is that, first of
all, I mean, listen, again, Biden is not an

00:01:40.139 --> 00:01:46.060
ultra progressive if Biden gets to do what
he's proposing.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.369
It will be the most progressive environmental
plan in the history of the United States.

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:53.549
Now you're going to have people who come out
and say he'll never get it done.

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:55.270
Well, that's not unique to Biden.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:58.219
No president gets everything done that they
say they want to do.

00:01:58.219 --> 00:02:02.549
You'll hear people come out and say, Biden
doesn't really believe this stuff.

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:05.639
He's only saying it because he thinks it will
help him politically.

00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:07.619
You can say that about any candidate.

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:10.140
And to some degree, it's always true.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:14.030
But the idea that Biden is particularly dishonest
about what he wants.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:15.450
I've seen no evidence for.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.970
So listen up.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.200
If I do a full review, I could come back to
you and say, here's the five things that aren't

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.600
in it that should be.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.540
But overall, I like that Biden has stuck to
his word of using the Green New Deal as a

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.480
framework for putting together a plan.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.860
I'm pleased with it.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.940
Fellow Trevor from I'm sorry I missed that
last part.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:39.940
I'm sorry.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:44.420
I'm pleased overall that Joe Biden has stuck
to his word and used the Green New Deal as

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.910
a framework for his plan.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:51.840
Yes, I agree completely that the Green New
Deal is a great framework, it should be what

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:52.840
we have.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:56.150
But this is definitely a great alternative.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:01.480
My second question really quickly would be,
do we need the Electoral College in order

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:05.900
or rather in order to implement rank choice
voting into our voting system?

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:09.760
Do we need the Electoral College or can we.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.230
Should we get rid of it in order to implement
rank choice?

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.230
You can do.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.970
Then we surveyed ungulate pipes.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.260
It's really two separate things.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:22.250
I mean, listen, if you go to national popular
vote, you eliminate electors per state and

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:29.420
you can tally the national popular vote as
first past the post or ranked choice voting,

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:31.420
single transferable vote, et cetera.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.050
There'd be one path.

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:37.200
The other path is you keep the Electoral College.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.770
But at the individual state level, the elections
are held using a ranked choice or alternative

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:43.770
voting system.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:47.010
So there's a lot of people talk about doing
both together.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:50.700
Obviously, it's incredibly unlikely that you're
going to get both together nationally at the

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.880
exact same time, but they don't have to both
be done together.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:54.880
OK, awesome.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.290
Thanks for answering my questions.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.810
All right, Trevor, thank you so much for the
phone call.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.000
